{"version":"ai-mcq-bank-v2-la-batch15-high-quality-rewritten-affected-2026-05-22-stem-fixed-inequality-rendering-fixed-student-facing-qc-2026-05-31-pt-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch2-foundations-counting-2026-06-11-pt-batch3-counting-probability-rules-2026-06-11-pt-batch4-conditioning-2026-06-11-pt-batch5-random-variables-2026-06-11-pt-batch6-discrete-distributions-2026-06-11-pt-batch7-distribution-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch8-continuous-expectation-2026-06-11-pt-batch9-non-week7-expectation-transform-2026-06-11-pt-batch10-non-week7-process-summary-2026-06-11-pt-batch11-non-week7-final-summary-shape-2026-06-11-quality-round1-2026-06-14-quality-round2-2026-06-14-quality-round3-2026-06-14-quality-round4-deep-2026-06-14+quality-round5-difficulty-2026-06-14+quality-round6-expression-2026-06-14+quality-round7-answer-cue-2026-06-14+quality-round8-answer-shape-2026-06-14+quality-round9-answer-position-2026-06-14+quality-round10-template-padding-2026-06-14+quality-round11-generic-stems-2026-06-14+quality-round12-deterministic-cleanup-2026-06-15+quality-pilot-deep-rework-2026-06-15+v3-2026-10-04+upright-2026-10-04+v3-2026-10-04+v3-2026-10-06+v3-2026-10-06+qa-fixes-2026-10-08","concept_id":"Year-1/2b-Probability-Distributions/conditional-probability-mass-function.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/2b-Probability-Distributions/conditional-probability-mass-function.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For discrete $X$ and $Y$ and a value $y$ with $p_Y(y)>0$, how is $p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$ defined?","options":["$p_{X,Y}(x,y)/p_X(x)$","$p_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,p_Y(y)$","$p_{X,Y}(x,y)/p_Y(y)$","$p_X(x)/p_Y(y)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3c84b09416f564ca5090cc47","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For discrete $X,Y$, suppose $0<p_Y(y)<1$ and $p_{X,Y}(u,y)=2p_{X,Y}(v,y)>0$, where $u\\ne v$. What is $p_{X\\mid Y}(u\\mid y)/p_{X\\mid Y}(v\\mid y)$?","options":["$2$","$2p_Y(y)$","$2/p_Y(y)$","$1/2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0691876cb28903cbf562566b","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For a value $y$ with $p_Y(y)>0$, which sum always equals $1$?","options":["$\\sum_y p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$","$\\sum_x\\sum_y p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$","$\\sum_y p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)\\,p_Y(y)$","$\\sum_x p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"04e24cd0dbc35b28b69dc36a","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Discrete $X,Y$ satisfy $p_Y(7)=0$. A student writes $p_{X\\mid Y}(2\\mid7)=0$ because $p_{X,Y}(2,7)=0$. How should this calculation be assessed?","options":["The result is $0$ because the numerator is $0$","The result is undefined because the ratio is $0/0$","The result is $p_X(2)$ because $Y=7$ never occurs","The result is $1$ because all possible cases are excluded"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3552b5d2f3491abea0fd0627","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For $p_Y(y)>0$, how does $p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$ compare with $p_{X,Y}(x,y)$?","options":["It is never smaller","It is never larger","They are always equal","Either can be larger"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3412a204f7500e3e5e3a3c65","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"A joint mass function has $p(0,0)=0.05$, $p(0,1)=0.15$, $p(0,2)=0.20$, $p(1,0)=0.15$, $p(1,1)=0.25$, $p(1,2)=0.20$, where $p(x,y)=\\mathbb{P}(X=x,Y=y)$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X=1\\mid Y=1)$?","options":["$0.25$","$0.6$","$0.625$","$\\tfrac5{12}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b5be488f0551710dfef99620","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Two fair coins are tossed independently; $X$ is the number of heads and $Y=1$ if the first coin shows heads, $Y=0$ otherwise. What is the conditional mass function of $X$ given $Y=1$, listed in the order $0,1,2$?","options":["$(\\tfrac14,\\tfrac12,\\tfrac14)$","$(0,\\tfrac14,\\tfrac14)$","$(0,1,0)$","$(0,\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dce713f4fa30f730ef27e5a4","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X\\in\\{0,2,5\\}$ and let $Y$ be discrete. Write $p(x,y)=\\mathbb{P}(X=x,Y=y)$. If $p(0,4)=0.14$, $p(2,4)=0.21$ and $p(5,4)=0.35$, what is $\\mathbb{P}(X\\ge2\\mid Y=4)$?","options":["$0.56$","$0.8$","$0.2$","$0.5$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9b672a25ca354f4620d55798","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Suppose $p_Y(2)=0.3$ and $p_{X\\mid Y}(5\\mid2)=0.4$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X=5,Y=2)$?","options":["$0.12$","$0.3$","$0.4$","$0.036$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8628cb82e49708c0cf1b3d6e","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $Y\\sim\\operatorname{Bin}(2,\\tfrac12)$ and $X=2Y$. What is the conditional mass function of $X$ given $Y=1$?","options":["The $\\operatorname{Bin}(2,\\tfrac12)$ mass function","Mass $\\tfrac12$ at $x=2$ and $\\tfrac12$ at $x=0$","Mass $1$ at $x=2$","Uniform on $\\{0,2,4\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c7671ac25e282003a08df80c","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In a joint table, the conditional mass functions $p_{X\\mid Y}(\\cdot\\mid y)$ coincide for every $y$ with $p_Y(y)>0$. What follows?","options":["$X$ and $Y$ are independent","$X$ and $Y$ are uncorrelated, but may be dependent","$X$ and $Y$ have the same distribution","$Y$ is a function of $X$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e40f6ff5f2b032345072d989","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"With $p_Y(1)=0.2$ and $p_Y(2)=0.6$, which expression gives $\\mathbb{P}(X=x\\mid Y\\in\\{1,2\\})$ in terms of $p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid1)$ and $p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid2)$?","options":["$\\tfrac12p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid1)+\\tfrac12p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid2)$","$\\tfrac14p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid1)+\\tfrac34p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid2)$","$0.2\\,p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid1)+0.6\\,p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid2)$","$p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid1)+p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid2)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5724b1ffdb56b3e28d99cfb9","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X\\in\\{1,\\dots,6\\}$ have mass function $p_X$, with $\\mathbb{P}(X\\text{ is even})>0$. Set $Y=0$ for even $X$ and $Y=1$ for odd $X$. What is $p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid0)$?","options":["$p_X(x)$ at both even and odd values of $x$","$p_X(x)/\\mathbb{P}(X\\text{ is even})$ at even $x$, and $0$ at odd $x$","$1/3$ at even values of $x$, and $0$ at odd values","$p_X(x)$ times $\\mathbb{P}(X\\text{ is even})$, kept on even values only"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"111ebcb314e52ab85edeaa7a","time_limit":45},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X,Y$ be independent with $\\mathbb{P}(X=j)=\\mathbb{P}(Y=j)=(1-p)^{j-1}p$ for integers $j\\ge1$, where $0<p<1$. For an integer $n\\ge2$, what is $\\mathbb{P}(X=k\\mid X+Y=n)$ for $1\\le k\\le n-1$?","options":["$(1-p)^{k-1}p$","$\\binom{n-1}{k}p^k(1-p)^{n-1-k}$","$\\tfrac kn$","$\\tfrac1{n-1}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6aff2deb339ffcc9dc162683","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Two fair six-sided dice are rolled independently. Given that the smaller score is $2$, what is the probability that the larger score is $5$?","options":["$\\tfrac15$","$\\tfrac14$","$\\tfrac29$","$\\tfrac2{36}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a1aae8c4e3fb993bbfaf8e8c","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $p_{X,Y}(x,y)=(x+y)/12$ for $x,y\\in\\{1,2\\}$, and zero elsewhere. Which formula gives $p_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$ for $x,y\\in\\{1,2\\}$?","options":["$\\dfrac{x+y}{12}$","$\\dfrac{x+y}{3+2y}$","$\\dfrac12$","$\\dfrac{x+y}{2x+3}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4c5b91b9909bf37e63b501ec","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For discrete $X,Y$ and one fixed value $x_0$, suppose $p_{X\\mid Y}(x_0\\mid y)\\ge p_X(x_0)$ for every $y$ with $p_Y(y)>0$. Which conclusion must hold?","options":["The joint table factorises into its marginals","$p_X(x_0)=1$","At least one of these conditional masses is strictly greater than $p_X(x_0)$","Every one of these conditional masses equals $p_X(x_0)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ad2cb0316aba63377ff1faf9","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A joint table has $p_{X,Y}(1,1)=0$ while $p_X(1)>0$ and $p_Y(1)>0$. What follows?","options":["Independence cannot be determined","$X$ and $Y$ are independent","$X$ and $Y$ are dependent","The table cannot be a valid joint mass function"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"988bdf377b8eeae75ede737f","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X\\sim\\operatorname{Pois}(2)$ and $Y=1$ if $X\\ge1$, $Y=0$ otherwise. What is $\\mathbb{E}[X\\mid Y=1]$?","options":["$\\tfrac2{1-\\mathrm{e}^{-2}}$","$2$","$3$","$2(1-\\mathrm{e}^{-2})$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"700e1fc033856bd08671a079","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_probability_mass_function_db21a844_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Let $Y$ be uniform on $\\{1,2,3\\}$ and, given $Y=y$, let $X$ be uniform on $\\{1,\\dots,y\\}$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(Y=3\\mid X=1)$?","options":["$\\tfrac13$","$\\tfrac19$","$\\tfrac6{11}$","$\\tfrac2{11}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d77946bb3c74cf5bea923cdf","time_limit":40}]}}